(4432262, 635916, 66384, '<td valign="top">Brian, I really like this image. I gave it a 7 during voting. I thought you had used a gradient map adjustment layer to get the effect. I often play with that layer myself. It''s interesting to read about your processing. At any rate, no matter how you did it, I like the product. It would be great in very large format on a wall in a modern loft.</td>', 'Brian, I really like this image. I gave it a 7 during voting. I thought you had used a gradient map adjustment layer to get the effect. I often play with that layer myself. It''s interesting to read about your processing. At any rate, no matter how you did it, I like the product. It would be great in very large format on a wall in a modern loft.', '2008-01-28 10:18:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4432267, 634982, 51538, '<td valign="top">It was hard not to vote any semi-competent image in this challenge with a six.  (Hopefully no one is going to come up with the idea of challenge: 10!).  I gave yours a 7.  I liked the everyday journalism of this image.  As a purist, it''s a pity the blur is not lens induced.  But I can understand why you had to add it in.</td>', 'It was hard not to vote any semi-competent image in this challenge with a six.  (Hopefully no one is going to come up with the idea of challenge: 10!).  I gave yours a 7.  I liked the everyday journalism of this image.  As a purist, it''s a pity the blur is not lens induced.  But I can understand why you had to add it in.', '2008-01-28 10:20:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4432347, 635921, 65319, '<td valign="top">I love the deep rich colors, the diagonal and the graduated DOF on the middle diagonal.  I didn''t see the six''s at first because the design and the colors are just brilliant and I was captured by the composition!</td>', 'I love the deep rich colors, the diagonal and the graduated DOF on the middle diagonal.  I didn''t see the six''s at first because the design and the colors are just brilliant and I was captured by the composition!', '2008-01-28 10:35:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4432369, 634982, 42196, '<td valign="top">This was my 2nd place image (my top pick finished 41st).<br/>By the title I wondered if this was a CBUS shot and was surprised to see it was you, Tim, as you say it is a different kind of image for you.<br/>The blur could have worked, especially with the sepia and the aspect ratio - it exudes a large format print feel.<br/>But as has been said, the blurring was not executed as well as it needed to get top votes.<br/>You should check out the Tiffen DFX package - it has a really great selective lens blur tool a la` Lensbabies.<br/>Would be interesting to see the results it would have on your original.<br/> <br/>Nice job, go CBUS! ;)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-28 10:44:09.</i></td>', 'This was my 2nd place image (my top pick finished 41st).By the title I wondered if this was a CBUS shot and was surprised to see it was you, Tim, as you say it is a different kind of image for you.The blur could have worked, especially with the sepia and the aspect ratio - it exudes a large format print feel.But as has been said, the blurring was not executed as well as it needed to get top votes.You should check out the Tiffen DFX package - it has a really great selective lens blur tool a la` Lensbabies.Would be interesting to see the results it would have on your original. Nice job, go CBUS! ;)', '2008-01-28 10:43:23.000000', '2008-01-28 10:44:09.000000', 0),
(4432375, 635535, 42196, '<td valign="top">thought this would have been top 10 for sure</td>', 'thought this would have been top 10 for sure', '2008-01-28 10:45:15.000000', NULL, 0),
